  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OCP Phosphogypsum</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The most significant, expected project-level outcome is to store phosphogypsum (PG) instead of discharging it into the ocean via outfalls,  and to enable future valorization options that could improve resource preservation. Beyond these project outcomes, IFC anticipates that its financing will promote competitiveness in fertilizers industry through introducing a necessary step for future valorization of PG that can be scaled via replication channels.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed investment consists of a corporate debt facility to OCP SA (OCP or the Company,&#xa0; https://www.ocpgroup.ma/ ) to finance the development of an inland phosphogypsum (PG) storage facility of up to 22 million tons capacity capacity, with a storage height of 60 m, in Jorf Lasfar, Morocco (the Project). OCP generates PG as a by-product in the production of phosphoric acid for phosphate fertilizers. The Project helps support sustainable PG management.</narrative>
  </description>
